<h2>Responsive Disable</h2>
<p>Disables a form field while it's hidden by responsive CSS — here, a plain <code>@media (max-width: 700px)</code> rule — so it isn't submitted, and re-enables it once visible again.</p>
<p><strong>Resize your browser window narrower than 700px</strong> (or open dev tools' device toolbar) to hide the promo code field below, then submit the form. The output shows exactly what was submitted — with the promo code missing once the field is hidden.</p>

<div class="demo-box" data-controller="demo-form-data">
  <form data-action="submit->demo-form-data#show">
    <label for="name">Name</label>
    <input id="name" type="text" name="user[name]" value="Ada Lovelace" />
    <br>

    <div class="responsive-disable-field" data-controller="responsive-disable">
      <label for="promo">Promo code <small>(hidden below 700px)</small></label>
      <input
        id="promo"
        type="text"
        name="user[promo_code]"
        value="WELCOME10"
        data-responsive-disable-target="field"
      />
    </div>

    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>

  <pre class="responsive-disable-output" data-demo-form-data-target="output">Submit the form to see the encoded data here.</pre>
</div>
